  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 225 PM Tuesday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Rain is likely across the southeastern United \nStates this weekend, with the best chance for central North Carolina \noccurring Sunday and Sunday night.\n\nAs of 2pm Tuesday, the National Hurricane Center \nwas tracking a broad area of thunderstorms over the southwestern \nGulf, giving this near a 100 percent chance to form a tropical \nsystem in the next 48 hours. Even if this does not become a tropical \nsystem, computer models are in very good agreement bringing the low \ncenter to the north through the rest of the work week, with the \nsystem likely moving onshore somewhere along the Gulf Coast Saturday \nand continuing to move north. While it is still too early to get \ninto the details for central North Carolina, it appears that much of \nSaturday should be dry, with the chance for rain increasing Saturday \nnight and likely peaking on Sunday, with rainfall decreasing Monday \nand Monday night. The current forecast calls for less than a 10% \nchance of 40 mph wind gusts locally.",
